= Web server — Technical =

Web-server deployments can terminate transport security, route requests by authority/path, generate dynamic representations, apply caching rules, and delegate to upstream applications. Reverse proxies and gateways can separate public HTTP handling from application execution.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* web server ≠ physical machine necessarily
* web server ≠ website
* server response ≠ static file necessarily

== References ==
* IETF RFC 9110, ''HTTP Semantics'' (2022), origin-server terminology.
* W3C, ''Architecture of the World Wide Web, Volume One'', server/agent interaction model.
